## 1. Question and answer form
Question: how can basic molecular properties be extracted and analysed from a chemical dataset?
The design answers it in three claims that a run could support or refute:
  C1 EXTRACTION  a descriptor layer turns one-row-per-molecule SMILES into a tidy, typed,
     complete property table with zero silent failures.
  C2 CORRECTNESS extracted values agree with pre-fixed independent references (hard gate).
  C3 ANALYSIS    the table supports interpretable distributional, correlational and subgroup
     statements, auditable back to individual molecules.

## 2. Input schema (portable; this is the contract, not the data)
One row per molecule, CSV/TSV, header required:
  id       str unique non-empty
  name     str optional label
  stratum  str optional; subgroup key ('druglike'|'extreme')
  smiles   str REQUIRED, canonical or isomeric SMILES, one molecule per row
  formula  str optional; if present it is a cross-check, never a source of truth
  <expected_*>  optional pre-declared reference columns, used only by the control table
Swap rule: a public set (ChEMBL / BDDS / PubChem subset export) drops in unchanged if it
projects onto {id, smiles} with smiles >=99% non-empty. Code, controls and analyses are
unchanged; only the expected-value columns must be regenerated, since they are curated
against THIS 47-molecule instance.
Instance used here: ./MOLECULES.csv -- 47 analyzable rows (20 druglike, 27 extreme/edge)
plus 5 negative-control rows. Curated by hand; no external dataset was available or needed.

## 3. Descriptor layer (pinned)
Environment contract: CPython >=3.9, rdkit >=2023.09; record exact version+build at run time
(python -c "from rdkit import Chem; print(Chem.rdmol.__version__)") and sha256 of the input
CSV. pandas optional (I/O only), numpy optional (correlations only). No GPU, no network.

Property -> exact call (all from one Mol object; never re-parse per descriptor):
  heavy_atoms      mol.GetNumHeavyAtoms()
  MW_avg           Descriptors.MolWt
  MW_monoisotopic  Descriptors.ExactMolWt        (MolWt is NOT this; a classic mix-up)
  formula          rdMolDescriptors.CalcMolFormula(mol)
  formal_charge    Chem.GetFormalCharge(mol)     (net, over all fragments)
  n_charged_atoms  sum(a.GetFormalCharge()!=0 for a in mol.GetAtoms())
  n_HBD            rdMolDescriptors.CalcNumHBD(mol)
  n_HBA            rdMolDescriptors.CalcNumHBA(mol)
  TPSA             rdMolDescriptors.CalcTPSA(mol)
  n_rot            rdMolDescriptors.CalcNumRotatableBonds(mol)  # DEFINITION IS
                                        # VERSION-DEPENDENT: pin the version, report it
  n_rings          rdMolDescriptors.CalcNumRings(mol)
  n_arom_rings     rdMolDescriptors.CalcNumAromaticRings(mol)
  n_heteroatoms    rdMolDescriptors.CalcNumHeteroatoms(mol)
  frac_CSP3        rdMolDescriptors.CalcFractionCSP3(mol)
  clogP            Descriptors.MolLogP(mol)      # Crippen estimate, a model output
