easurement. It is labelled an estimate\n    and is never used as ground truth for a molecule's real lipophilicity.\nFailure contract (the load-bearing engineering decision):\n  Chem.MolFromSmiles(smi) returns None on parse failure. On None the pipeline MUST raise and\n  record (id, reason). It must never emit a row of zeros, never silently coerce to NaN, and\n  never continue a batch. Rationale: zeros are indistinguishable from a molecule with\n  genuinely zero HBD/HBA/TPSA, so the corruption is invisible in every downstream statistic.\n  NEG1-NEG5 exist to keep this honest.\nCanonical round-trip: canonical = Chem.MolToSmiles(mol); re-parse and re-describe; the two\ndescriptor vectors must be bit-identical.\nEOF\nwc -l DESIGN.md", "exit_code": 0, "timed_out": false, "elapsed_seconds": 0.065, "output": "64 DESIGN.md\n", "output_truncated": false}"}], "is_error": false, "kind": "BenchmarkObservation"}, "action_id": "a1b360e8-2e0b-4a8d-ab7d-5bec1f597f80", "extended_content": [], "kind": "ObservationEvent"}
