     HBD/HBA/TPSA (expected 1/2 vs 2/1). No tautomer standardisation is applied.
     EXPECTED: values DIFFER. If they come out identical, the descriptor layer is not doing
     what we assume. If they differ, A3/A5 must not treat tautomers as independent chemistry
     without an explicit caveat.
  K8 stereo-insensitivity. B24 L-alanine vs B25 D-alanine: every achiral descriptor must be
     identical. Failure mode: a descriptor that accidentally encodes chirality, breaking the
     subgroup pooling in A3.
  K9 version reproducibility. Re-run on a second pinned RDKit minor version. Expected:
     MW/formula/heavy/charge/HBD/HBA/TPSA/rings identical; n_rot and frac_CSP3 explicitly
     diffed because their definitions have changed across releases. Disagreement in the first
     group is an environment problem, never a finding.
  K10 round-trip idempotence. canonical SMILES -> re-parse -> descriptors equal the originals
     for 47/47.
DISCONFIRMING EVIDENCE (pre-declared; what would make us abandon the pipeline):
  * any molecule whose MW_avg disagrees with the formula arithmetic beyond tolerance AND
    survives re-parsing from a hand-written molblock -> toolkit usage wrong, or the input
    column is not SMILES;
  * any negative control yielding a value instead of an error -> the failure contract is
    broken, and EVERY downstream mean/distribution is suspect because silent zeros bias them;
  * benzene reporting TPSA > 0 or n_arom_rings = 0 -> aromaticity perception is off, which
    invalidates n_arom_rings, clogP and TPSA across the whole table;
  * round-trip descriptors differing for >=1 molecule -> the table is not reproducible and
    must not be shared;
  * L- and D-alanine differing on any achiral descriptor -> sanitisation/atom-order
    nondeterminism, i.e. extraction is not a function of the molecule.
EOF
