## 5. Analysis plan (all thresholds fixed before any run)
Scope: n=47 analyzable rows, 2 hand-defined strata (20 druglike / 27 extreme). Everything
below is DESCRIPTIVE. No p-value is reported as a finding anywhere in this design.
  A1 Distributions. median [IQR], min, max, 5th-95th percentile for MW, clogP, TPSA, n_rot;
     integer counts as frequency tables. Skew-prone columns (MW, TPSA, clogP) additionally
     shown log-scaled so shape claims are not scale-dependent.
     Reference arithmetic for the MW column (from ./shadow_check.py, EXPECTED):
     n=47, min 46.07, max 393.73, median 132.12, mean 154.92, sd 81.39. A run whose MW
     summary drifts materially from this has an extraction problem, not a chemistry story.
     CAVEAT printed alongside every distribution: this set is NOT a random chemical sample;
     its shape describes the curation, not any population. No population inference is made.
  A2 Redundancy / collinearity (kept because it controls interpretation).
     Spearman rho over MW, heavy_atoms, TPSA, (HBD+HBA), n_rot, frac_CSP3.
     EXPECTED: MW~heavy_atoms rho >= 0.95 (arithmetic, not discovery); TPSA~(HBD+HBA) high;
     MW~TPSA high. PRE-DECLARED CONSEQUENCE: these are collinear by construction, so they are
     reported as ONE size/polarity axis and never as independent risk factors; a rule-of-five
     screen is reported as a sum of parts, not four findings.
     Diagnostic use: MW~heavy_atoms near 0 would indicate descriptor columns misaligned across
     rows -- a cheap catch for data-join bugs.
  A3 Subgroup contrasts -- DESCRIPTIVE ONLY (scope guard honoured).
     Contrasts: druglike vs extreme; |charge|>0 or internal charges vs neutral; HBD=0 vs >0;
     n_arom_rings=0 vs >=1.
     Reported per contrast: group medians and IQRs, Hodges-Lehmann shift estimate,
     rank-biserial effect size, and fraction of distributional overlap. Mann-Whitney U is
     COMPUTED BUT PRE-DECLARED LOW-POWERED AND NON-REPORTABLE as a finding at n~20/27; it is
