dance rounding for B/Si/Cl/S.", "Whether you want the A4 coverage gap closed by adding >500 Da and >10-HBA molecules (I documented the limitation and the fix rather than silently expanding the set).", "The 0.80 floor on rho(MW,heavy) is set to stay far below 0.868 while remaining above any plausible mis-join; it is a judgment call, not a derived constant.", "If RDKit is later made available, executing PIPELINE_SPEC.py would convert this design into an actual experiment — I have deliberately not simulated that outcome."], "kind": "ReviewHandoffAction"}, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a744d35f484c2286", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-a744d35f484c2286", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{"answer": "DESIGN COMPLETE (design-only; no experiment executed, no results claimed). Deliverables in /workspace/design/: DESIGN.md (257 lines, 8 sections), MOLECULES.csv (52 rows = 47 analyzable + 5 negative controls), PIPELINE_SPEC.py (executable spec, refuses to run without RDKit), shadow_check.py + CONTROL_HARNESS_DRYRUN.py (stdlib-only, actually run \u2014 design verification, not chemistry).\n\nAPPROACH. Question answered as three refutable claims: C1 extraction (SMILES \u2192 tidy typed table, zero silent failures), C2 correctness (agreement with pre-fixed independent references), C3 analysis (auditable distributional/correlational/subgroup statements).\n\nDATA + SCHEMA. Portable contract {id, name?, stratum?, smiles (required), formula? (cross-check only)}; any public set drops in if it projects onto {id,smiles} at \u226599% non-empty; only expected-value columns need regeneration. Instance: 20 druglike + 27 extreme/edge, incl. deliberate tautomer pair (2-hydroxypyridine/2-pyridone), enantiomer pair (L/D-alanine), ions/zwitterion/salt, halogen-rich, macrocycles, plus 5 parse-failure rows.\n\nDESCRIPTOR LAYER (pinned). 15 RDKit calls named exactly (MolWt vs ExactMolWt distinguished; CalcNumRotatableBonds flagged version-dependent). HBD/HBA pinned to RDKit Lipinski SMARTS with explicit warning not to mix toolkits. clogP labelled a Crippen estimate, never ground truth. Failure contract is the load-bearing decision: MolFromSmiles\u2192None MUST raise and record a reason; never emit zeros \u2014 because zeros are indistinguishable from legitimate zero descriptors, corrupting every downstream statistic invisibly. Plus canonical round-trip identity.\n\nCONTROLS K1\u2013K10, each with expected value + named failure mode, plus the requested disconfirming section. K1 (MW vs hand-audited formula arithmetic, tolerance 0.05/0.10 for B\u00b7Si) is the hard gate and stops the run; recalled logP values are quarantined to plausibility bands and rank order and can never fail the pipeline, per your instruction.\n\nSTATISTICAL HONESTY. All contrasts descriptive: medians/IQRs, Hodges\u2013Lehmann shift, rank-biserial, overlap fraction. Mann\u2013Whitney U computed but pre-declared low-powered and NON-REPORTABLE as a finding at n\u224820/27. MW\u2194heavy-atoms\u2194TPSA collinearity retained as an interpretation control (reported as ONE size/polarity axis, never independent risk factors).\n\nWHAT I ACTUALLY VERIFIED (design verification, not results). (1) shadow_check.py cross-checks each SMILES atom census against an independently written formula: 47/47 agreement after corrections. (2) CONTROL_HARNESS_DRYRUN.py injects a mock descriptor function into the real harness and sabotages it: happy path trips nothing; MW +3 Da \u2192 K1 hard stop; MW +0.02 Da \u2192 correctly does NOT trip (tolerance meaningful, not vacuous); simulated try/except-returning-zeros \u2192 K4 trips, overall_pass False; round-trip drift \u2192 K10 raises; all 5 negatives rejected by the correct harness yet passing silently under the sabotaged one. It also correctly reports NEG4 (pentavalent carbon) as NOT stdlib-detectable, assigned to RDKit sanitisation.\n\nFIVE DESIGN ERRORS MY OWN CHECKS CAUGHT (all fixed, a