     0.893 and the constant in PIPELINE_SPEC.py was updated with the reason recorded; A1 MW
     summary updated to n=51 (max 393.73 -> 712.16, sd 81.39 -> 137.37).
  4. Added the requested coverage matrix (7.6), LIVE / WEAK / NOT LIVE per control and per
     analysis step, each with what to add if the step matters, plus the explicit rule that a
     "pass" on a WEAK or NOT LIVE row is not evidence.
  5. Writing the matrix exposed a false claim I had asserted rather than checked: I wrote
     that rule-of-three was inert because all rows exceed 300 Da. The data says 44 of 51 are
     UNDER 300 Da, so the Ro3 size axis is live (44/7 split) -- and interestingly three of
     the seven failures (iodoform, omeprazole, warfarin) are ordinary drugs. Corrected in
     both the matrix and A4, with the error left visible rather than silently overwritten.
