place and logged in \u00a79.5.\n\nFINAL SWEEP: py_compile OK for all three modules; data 56 rows, strata {druglike 20, extreme 27, boundary 4, negative 5}, 56 unique ids; DESIGN.md checks all OK (option-(a) stated, coverage matrix present with LIVE/WEAK/NOT LIVE, zero stale \"47 analyzable rows\" claims, C01\u2013C04 referenced, K1\u2013K10 defined, DISCONFIRMING EVIDENCE present, DESIGN ONLY + \"NOT experimental results\" guards present); 4 boundary rows present in CSV.\n\nTWO IMPLEMENTATION BUGS FOUND AND FIXED DURING THIS REVISION (disclosed rather than hidden): my CSV-insertion script's guard `if stratum=='negative' and not new_rows` was never true because earlier rows had already populated the list, so the first insertion silently wrote 0 boundary rows \u2014 caught only because I re-ran the verifier and saw n still 47, then added an `assert done` on the insertion point. A second script aborted on a nonsense `a.setdefault(...)` line. Neither corrupted the data file; both were caught before hand-off.", "assumptions": ["Option (a) chosen per reviewer's stated preference; the alternative (b) descope remains documented as a valid path in \u00a79's framing.", "Expected HBD/HBA/n_rot values for C01\u2013C04 are my hand-assigned pre-declarations under the pinned RDKit definitions, not measurements; borderline ones (C04 HBA=11, C02 HBA=11) sit close to the >10 cut and may land on either side.", "clogP>5 for C03 is asserted from qualitative reasoning about three C12 chains, not a computed estimate; flagged WEAK in the matrix for exactly that reason.", "The 4-row boundary stratum is sized to cross thresholds, not to estimate rates; per-axis counts are coverage evidence only.", "Average MW from CIAAW-2021 abridged atomic weights, as before; boundary formulas come from algebraic homolog expressions.", "Nothing executed as an experiment; RDKit remains absent and uninstallable here."], "uncertainties": ["C04 (sucrose) carries the highest SMILES risk in the whole set \u2014 t